</section></score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>In bondman’s form, with lowliness,</l><l>Thou walkedst on this earth of woe;</l><l>The human living Thou didst have</l><l>And all its suff’rings undergo.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Born in a manger as a babe,</l><l>Thou wast a child among the poor;</l><l>Thou as a carpenter didst work,</l><l>And e’en an outlaw’s death endure.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Then Thou wast raised up from the dead,</l><l>Still with the human nature true;</l><l>And as a man in form divine,</l><l>Thou didst ascend to heaven too.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Now over all, and on the throne,</l><l>Thou, still a man, art glorified;</l><l>A man with God in light divine</l><l>With whom our God is satisfied.</l></lg>
<lg label="6."><l>In glory Thou wilt come again,</l><l>Still as a man appearing then;</l><l>As King of kings, with pow’r divine,</l><l>With human nature seen by men.</l></lg>
<lg label="7."><l>Thou, as the center of all things,</l><l>In the new heav’n and earth shalt be,</l><l>Forever as the One divine,</l><l>Existing in humanity.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
